Description:

Description of Role:


As a Development Engineer, you will support the design and engineering of grid\-scale battery energy storage projects during the development phase, from initial site screening through concept design and handoff to execution. Reporting to Lightshift's Lead Development Engineer, you will help produce site layouts, preliminary electrical designs, equipment sizing, and interconnection deliverables that shape how our projects get built. You will also research emerging storage technologies and industry trends and support the development team with technical analysis. This role is a great opportunity for an ambitious self\-starter looking to help fuel the growth of one of the most innovative companies in the space.


Core responsibilities will include:

* Develop a comprehensive understanding of battery energy storage systems, their components, and how they are integrated into utility\-scale projects;
* Support concept design of energy storage projects, applying Lightshift's standardized and modular design principles to individual sites;
* Prepare site layouts, single\-line diagrams, and preliminary electrical and civil design documents;
* Perform equipment sizing and technology selection analysis based on project requirements, use case, and site constraints;
* Support interconnection applications and studies, including preparation of technical data and coordination with utilities;
* Assist with permitting deliverables and early\-stage regulatory and safety code compliance (e.g., NFPA 855, UL 9540A) review;
* Conduct research on emerging technologies, suppliers, and industry trends and summarize findings for the engineering team;
* Contribute to technical documentation, design basis reports, and specifications used to support project financing and procurement;
* Participate in project meetings and present technical information to internal stakeholders.


Location:

* Lightshift's Arlington, VA headquarters


